From: knulli
Subject: [PATCH] video: sunxi: disp2: enable the de iommu on a smooth boot too

The framebuffer comes from ion and is mapped behind the iommu, so its
smem_start is an iova (0xffc00000 here, while ram starts at 0x40000000).
disp_init_connections() only turns on translation for the display engine when
u-boot did NOT hand the display over (boot_info.sync == 0); after a smooth
handoff the engine fetches the iova as a physical address, so the panel shows
a constant colour no matter what is in the framebuffer, and /sys/class/disp/
disp/attr/sys reports iommu[0].

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/de/disp_display.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/de/disp_display.c
index 0ae409fd7..88d63aff1 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/de/disp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/de/disp_display.c
@@ -494,6 +494,15 @@ s32 disp_init_connections(struct disp_bsp_init_para *para)
 					}
 				}
 			}
+			/*
+			 * The framebuffer is allocated from ion and lives
+			 * behind the iommu, so the display engine needs
+			 * translation whether or not u-boot handed the display
+			 * over.  Without this the engine fetches the iova as a
+			 * physical address and the panel shows a constant
+			 * colour.
+			 */
+			mgr->enable_iommu(mgr, true);
 		} else if (para->boot_info.sync == 0) {
 			dispdev = disp_device_get(disp, DISP_OUTPUT_TYPE_LCD);
 			if ((dispdev) && (dispdev->set_manager))
